                      metered_light_count, represented_light_count, wattage, working_hours,
                      state, location, meter_installed_at, light_replacement_date,
                      pre_install_baseline, benchmark_savings_pct, eligibility_checklist,
                      created_by_id, created_at)
SELECT 'bf-rg-residency-ckt-1', s.id, 'bf-rg-residency-survey', 'lighting', 'basement',
       69, 1444, 20, 24,
       'benchmark_confirmed', 'Basement',
       '2025-09-06'::date, '2025-10-04'::date,
       32.69, 66.00,
       jsonb_build_object('backfilled', true, 'source', 'signed agreement + post-installation savings report',
                          'note', 'Commissioned before this system existed — CON-16 eligibility was never assessed.',
                          'deviations', '["eligibility-never-assessed", "dates-inferred-from-readings", "benchmark-mean-of-demo-percentages", "benchmark-rounded-in-agreement", "report-dates-contradict-its-tables"]'::jsonb,
                          'basisNote', 'TWO demos on two areas, both recorded against this one circuit because the agreement prices them as one: 49 stilt lights (22.67 -> 10.49 = 53.75%) and 20 basement lights (10.02 -> 2.13 = 78.75%). Their simple mean is 66.25%; the agreement''s own arithmetic gives 66.00%, so the benchmark is an override of a rounded figure. The consumption-weighted ratio would be 61.39% and is not used - same mean-of-percentages rule as Aditya Urban Casa. baseline/after are the two demos summed, 32.69 and 12.62. BOTH REPORTS'' PROSE CONTRADICTS THEIR OWN TABLES: each says the pre-installation window was ''(07-11 Oct 2025)'' while the tables list 22-25 Sep for the stilt demo and 07-11 Sep for the basement one. The tables are the data. Both are also headed ''Savings % w.r.t 20.24 kWh'', the same leftover French Apartment carries; each report''s own percentages only work against its own baseline. The stilt report marks every post-installation day ''Within Acceptable Range: No'' - its 53.75% sits well below the basement demo''s 78.75%, which is what the averaging resolves. All four tables reproduce their stated averages to 2dp. Neither date is stated: meter install taken as the day before the earliest reading of either demo (07 Sep 2025), replacement as the day before the later demo''s post-install readings start (05 Oct).'),
       a.id, now()
FROM societies s, admin_users a WHERE s.name = 'RG Residency' AND a.id = 'sys-data-import' ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
